[{"sha":"0844c208f683527c08ea8a80acc13b398aa9c8bf","node_id":"C_kwDOAaETR9oAKDA4NDRjMjA4ZjY4MzUyN2MwOGVhOGE4MGFjYzEzYjM5OGFhOWM4YmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"chrisdebian","email":"cjhandrew@gmail.com","date":"2026-04-08T08:56:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"Erik de Castro Lopo","email":"erikd@mega-nerd.com","date":"2026-08-13T02:47:19Z"},"message":"cmake: remove unused macros from config.h template\n\nSix macros defined in config.h.cmake are never referenced in any C or\nheader file in the library:\n\n  CPU_IS_LITTLE_ENDIAN, HAVE_LRINT, HAVE_LRINTF,\n  HAVE_STDINT_H, SIZEOF_INT, SIZEOF_LONG\n\nThese appear to be remnants from a time when libsamplerate provided its\nown lrint/lrintf fallbacks and portability shims for older compilers.\nThat code was removed, but the corresponding config.h entries were not.\n\nAlso remove the if(CPU_IS_BIG_ENDIAN)/set(CPU_IS_LITTLE_ENDIAN) block\nfrom CMakeLists.txt, which existed solely to populate the now-removed\nCPU_IS_LITTLE_ENDIAN entry.\n\nVerified by grepping all .c and .h files under src/ and include/:\nnone of the six symbols appear.","tree":{"sha":"aaeafa8675eca452a6b38dfa1918290e0e495137","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libsndfile/libsamplerate/git/trees/aaeafa8675eca452a6b38dfa1918290e0e495137"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libsndfile/libsamplerate/git/commits/0844c208f683527c08ea8a80acc13b398aa9c8bf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libsndfile/libsamplerate/commits/0844c208f683527c08ea8a80acc13b398aa9c8bf","html_url":"https://github.com/libsndfile/libsamplerate/commit/0844c208f683527c08ea8a80acc13b398aa9c8bf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libsndfile/libsamplerate/commits/0844c208f683527c08ea8a80acc13b398aa9c8bf/comments","author":{"login":"chrisdebian","id":17935223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTM1MjIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17935223?v=4","gravat